I'm still alive in this particular game, on Sokoban
top-level without having forgotten to eat somewhere
along the way, for once, but yeesh...

I had ESP and a dandy black silk blindfold "My
Mask", and having visited Mines Town rich and naive,
AC:-16 was looking pretty nice as a working kit, so
I dragged five pets (not always the same five) up
Sokoban with me, pushing boulders with great
confidence.

Only once did I double-type and isolate a boulder
against a wall, and by then the (top) level was
nearly solved anyway and it had boulders to spare.

Coming _up to_ the top level with its guaranteed two
giant mimics, though, I ran into a problem never
before encountered by me, thus worth documenting
here, and it caught two of my buff pets via my
slowness of wit.

Up the stairs to toplevel Sokoban I went, two pets
in tow, and there, right in front of me was a
misplaced boulder (== giant mimic), leaving my pets
standing beside it, them and it blocking me from
stepping away from the stairs.

----
|@`
|ff
----

I wasn't blind just then, so I wasn't seeing the
immediacy of the danger, nor the ongoing brief
conflict between "boulder" and immobile pets, just
waiting fat and stupid for my pets to clear out of
my way rather than me bully through them.

I typed "." twice to rest, and I was short two pets.

This is _not_ what I expected, and what I'm
describing may not even be what I saw, I was so in
shock, but I dagger-stormed the damned mimic to
death before going back down for the other three
pets.(*)

The RNG really, really got me that time, Two buffed
up HP72(72) pets gone in a flash before I'd seen at
all that they were in danger.

Take warning o ye players from this my woeful tale.

Go thou and do otherwise.

xanthian.

(*) [Carrying 22 daggers in quiver is a weight
headache, but _so_ nice for days where the RNG is
not your usual blithe friend and boon companion.

Twice in traversing Sokoban I've had to kill
monsters on the other side of Sokoban boulders, and
that's just, in the one case, where I wanted the
three chickatrices to stay, who greeted me on bottom
level Sokoban. Dagger storms work _great_ in those
cases; thanks to whomever told us that boulders were
transparent to missile weapons, an unexpected datum.

Trap doors that misplaced pets had forced me to
level up _a lot_ before I got to Sokoban, maybe XL:5
with Sokoban fairly deep, spanning DLVL7 to DLVL4,
thus the fighting has been a bit on the heavy side
and steadily expensive of newly acquired pets; I
even lost a warhorse once, though that may have been
due to its starvation.

My squad, reassembled after protection racketeering,
had done a great job on eliminating the Mines Town
watch, so my armor choices were profuse, and I have
a silver saber I hope to put to excellent use
someday.

I'm not looking forward _at all_ with much glee to
the trip to Mines End, and I've gotten this far
without IDing ?Identify, so I'm playing mostly in
the dark with the aid of two nice main dungeon (now
converted) altars for BUCing armor and blessing
water. The only scrolls known are Earth (from
Sokoban), Teleportation (I took a risk hoping a
blessed scroll in three copies was ?Identify) and
Create Monster (a monster read one).]



